    "faq_salmon": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_marinate": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long should I marinate miso salmon?",
            "text": "<p>The classic Nobu method calls for a full <strong>48 hours</strong>. The saké, miso, and coconut sugar need that time to fully penetrate the fillet, which is what creates the deep caramelization under the broiler. In a hurry? Even 24 hours delivers excellent flavor — but plan for two days if you can.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_temp": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What internal temperature should King Salmon be cooked to?",
            "text": "<p>Pull the salmon at around <strong>130°F</strong> for medium-rare. Residual heat will carry it to roughly 150°F as it rests for 3–5 minutes, giving you a tender, flaky finish without drying out the fillet. See our full <a href=\"/pages/the-ultimate-guide-to-salmon-internal-temp\" title=\"The Ultimate Guide to Salmon Internal Temp\">guide to salmon internal temp</a>.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_kingsalmon": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What makes King Salmon different from Atlantic salmon?",
            "text": "<p>King Salmon (<em>Oncorhynchus tshawytscha</em>, also called Chinook) is the largest and fattiest of the Pacific salmon species. That higher fat content means significantly more omega-3s, richer marbling, and a silkier texture — which is why it holds up so well to a 48-hour marinade and a hard broil.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_mealprep": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long do the bento boxes keep in the fridge?",
            "text": "<p>Sealed and refrigerated, the assembled bento boxes hold for <strong>3–4 days</strong>. The miso-glazed salmon is delicious warm or at room temperature, so there's no need to reheat. Our rhythm: defrost Friday morning, marinate Friday evening, assemble Sunday for the week ahead.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "question_defrost": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I defrost sushi-grade King Salmon?",
            "text": "<p>Defrost Seatopia seafood in the refrigerator overnight, wrapped in paper, to preserve nutrient integrity and texture. For a faster method, place the vacuum-sealed fish in a bowl of cold water for 30–60 minutes.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
